# title: Himalaya
# category: Multi-asset
# underlyings: 3
# source: Bouzoubaa & Osseiran, Exotic Options and Hybrids: A Guide to Structuring, Pricing and Trading, Wiley, 2010
# summary: Each year the best performer of the remaining stocks is locked in and removed; pays the average of the locked performances above 100%.
#
# Notional 1000, three stocks, three yearly observations. A removed stock
# gets a performance of -1000 so it can never be the best again.

2027-01-04
    s0 = spot(0)
    s1 = spot(1)
    s2 = spot(2)
    in0 = 1
    in1 = 1
    in2 = 1
    total = 0

2028-01-04  2029-01-04  2030-01-04
    q0 = in0 * spot(0) / s0 - (1 - in0) * 1000
    q1 = in1 * spot(1) / s1 - (1 - in1) * 1000
    q2 = in2 * spot(2) / s2 - (1 - in2) * 1000
    best = max(q0, max(q1, q2))
    total = total + best
    if q0 = best then
        in0 = 0
    else
        if q1 = best then in1 = 0 else in2 = 0 endIf
    endIf

2030-01-07
    pays 1000 * max(total / 3 - 1, 0)
